 "description": "T-4922: which missingCaption texts Excel shows as a number in a pivot's empty intersections, each sheet one builder-v2 pivot at A3 (rows Region, columns Product, Sum of Sales over Data!A1:C7) that Excel renders on open; the question cell of every sheet is D6, West by C, which no record reaches. gen-pivot shows a caption of a lone minus sign as the number 0 in the data field's format and n/a as text (pivots.md \"What the gen-pivot batch found\"). Z0 to Z10: captions a cell entry would read as a value: Z0 `0`, Z1 `1`, Z2 `-1`, Z3 `1.5`, Z4 `1e2`, Z5 `50%`, Z6 `$5`, Z7 `(1)`, Z8 `1/2`, Z9 `TRUE`, Z10 `1,000`. D0 to D10: what makes the minus sign zero: D0 `-`, D1 ` - `, D2 `- `, D3 `--`, D4 `+`, D5 `.`, D6 `—`, D7 `–`, D8 `'-`, D9 `-x`, D10 `x-` (D6 an em dash, D7 an en dash). E0: an empty caption (the T-4967 question). E1: showMissing with no caption. E2: the minus sign with showMissing off. E3: the minus sign under numFmtId 4 (#,##0.00). E4: under a Count data field. E5: under numFmtId 10 (0.00%). E6: `7` under numFmtId 4. E7: `n/a` under numFmtId 4. E8: `n/a` with showMissing off, and E9: no caption with showMissing off, to tell \"the flag is ignored\" from \"with the flag off Excel shows zeros whatever the caption\", which E2 alone cannot. Z11: `-0`. D11: `x`, a one-character caption that is neither sign nor digit. G: GETPIVOTDATA of West by C against D0, Z1, Z0, E1, E7, E0 and E9, to see whether the function answers the shown number or #REF!.",
